WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.020
STEPHANIE WONG:
Today, we're talking

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.550
about carbon-free energy, a
new podcast from our SREs,

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.550
and the ultimate
guide to speech AI.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.640
I'm Stephanie Wong, and welcome
to "This Week on Cloud," where

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.090
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.370
Securing around the
clock carbon-free energy

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.180
isn't just important for Google.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.960
It's also critical for the
world to successfully tackle

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.090
the urgent challenge
of climate change.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.760
While rapid progress and
cost-effective carbon-free

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.860
energy technology
has put the prospect

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.290
of decarbonized electricity
grids within reach,

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.600
it's not inevitable.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.300
And that's why we are committed
to working with stakeholders

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.200
across the globe to advocate for
policies that accelerate grid

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.480
decarbonization for everyone.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.110
Check out the blog to join us.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.730
We're excited to announce
the launch of the Google SRE

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.260
prodcast, an interview
style podcast

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.840
where site reliability
engineers at Google

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.360
discuss key SRE
concepts and share

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:00.440
their experiences, advice, and
strong opinions, along the way.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.170
Since early 2016,
SREs at Google had

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.780
been producing and listening
to an internal version

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.170
of the podcast.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.430
This year, we decided to think
bigger and share insights

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:15.490
from Google SREs with
the wider SRE community.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.760
Thanks to AI, speaking out
loud has become not only

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.270
a primary way of communicating
with machines, like when

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:24.040
you tell your smartphone
to send a text

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.440
or ask your smart speaker
about the weather,

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.330
but also enriching
human interactions,

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:31.930
such as generating
captions in near real time

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.520
during a video meeting.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.770
Head to the blog to
explore some of the most

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:38.440
interesting and practical
applications of speech

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.540
technology as well
as the Google Cloud

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.197
tools that make building
these sorts of apps possible.

00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:47.280
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.320
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.140
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:55.790
We'll see you in the Cloud.

